icons.json records source paths and hashes. tools/import_aosp_icons.py reproduces imports.

Classic (newStatusBarIcons=false) WifiIcons and SignalDrawable variants are used.
Wi-Fi, ethernet and globe assets are copied verbatim. Cellular normal assets retain
upstream paths and add autoMirrored to match SignalDrawable's RTL behavior.
Cellular no-internet assets bake SignalDrawable.STATE_CUT using config.xml:
config_signalCutoutWidthFraction=7, config_signalCutoutHeightFraction=17,
config_signalAttributionPath=M20,10h2v8h-2z M20,20h2v2h-2z.
SignalDrawable clears the bottom-right 7x17 area of its 24x24 canvas and draws
this attribution path; vectors achieve the same geometry with a notched polygon clip.

No runtime dependency on SettingsLib, internal resource IDs, or hidden APIs.

